# 1N5819 Schottky diode.
#
# A metal-semiconductor junction: it conducts at a few tenths of a volt where a
# silicon diode needs about 0.7, which is why it guards supplies and catches
# inductive kicks. PHYSICS only, with the 1N5819's model numbers.
#
# Drawn by the `diode_1n5819` painter: the rectifier's DO-41 paths from the
# PinBench Parts Figma file, with a silver band.

PART "Schottky Diode (1N5819)"
ID diode_1n5819
CATEGORY basic
DESCRIPTION "1 A Schottky barrier diode, DO-41 — low forward drop"

# Standing on its leads, anode up: the tips are four hole pitches apart on
# the lattice, the cathode band toward the bottom one.
SIZE 40px 72px
PAINTER diode_1n5819

PINS
  anode    20px  4px   passive "A"
  cathode  20px  68px  passive "K"

PHYSICS diode
  n1 = anode
  n2 = cathode
  # SPICE model parameters: saturation current and emission coefficient.
  is = 31.7e-6
  n = 1.373
